{"extract": "Sir Christopher Robert Chope  (born 19 May 1947) is a British politician and former barrister who has served as the Member of Parliament (MP) for Christchurch in Dorset since 1997. A member of the Conservative Party, he was first elected in 1983 for Southampton Itchen, but lost this seat in 1992 to Labour. He returned to Parliament in 1997 and has remained an MP ever since.", "links": [{"ns": 0, "title": "1983 United Kingdom general election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "1992 United Kingdom general election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "1997 United Kingdom general election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Barrister", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bob Mitchell (British politician)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Christchurch (UK Parliament constituency)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Conservative Party (UK)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Diana Maddock", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Dorset", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "George Young, Baron Young of Cookham", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "ISBN (identifier)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Incumbent", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "John Denham (politician)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "John Major", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kenneth Carlisle", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Labour Party (UK)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Margaret Thatcher", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Member of Parliament (United Kingdom)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Officer of the Order of the British Empire", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Parliamentary Under-Secretary of State for Transport", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Parliamentary Under-Secretary of State for the Environment", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Patrick Nicholls", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Politicia